# AI Agency Website — Development Rules

## SOURCE OF TRUTH

The file:

AI_AGENCY_WEBSITE_MASTER_SPEC.md

is the primary source of truth for this project.

Read it before making major implementation decisions.

## BRAND

Core brand idea:

Unfair Operational Leverage.

The agency has two integrated capabilities:

1. AI Growth
2. AI Systems

## AI GROWTH

Includes:

- AI UGC
- AI product photography
- CGI product advertising
- Creative production
- Paid advertising
- Performance marketing

Never remove AI Growth or AI UGC.

## AI SYSTEMS

Includes:

- AI automation
- Agentic AI
- AI employees
- AI sales systems
- Lead qualification
- CRM automation
- Customer support
- AI chatbots
- AI voice agents
- Internal business automation
- Workflow automation
- RAG / knowledge systems

Never invent new services without approval.

## DESIGN

The website must feel:

- Editorial
- Premium
- Intelligent
- Technological
- Commercial
- Restrained

Avoid:

- Generic SaaS design
- Cyberpunk aesthetics
- Neon AI clichés
- Robot imagery
- Generic gradient cards
- Excessive particles
- Excessive animation
- Random 3D decoration

## DO NOT CHANGE

Do not redesign the brand.

Do not change the approved homepage narrative.

Do not silently change approved copy.

Do not remove sections because they appear technically difficult.

Do not remove AI Growth.

Do not remove AI UGC.

Do not change the agency architecture.

If something is technically problematic, explain the problem before changing the design.

## DEVELOPMENT

Use reusable components.

Keep the code maintainable.

Optimize for production performance.

Support:

- Desktop
- Tablet
- Mobile
- Reduced motion
- Accessibility

Do not sacrifice performance for visual effects.

## WORKFLOW

Before major implementation:

1. Read the relevant specification.
2. Explain the implementation approach.
3. Implement.
4. Test the result.
5. Review changes against the specification.
6. Report deviations.

Do not build the entire website in one uncontrolled operation.

## IMPORTANT

When a decision is unclear, do not invent an answer.

Ask for approval or clearly flag the decision.

Technical implementation must serve the approved design rather than redefine it.